--- a/CHANGES
+++ b/CHANGES
@@ -29,6 +29,16 @@ Version 3.3.3 - in development
 ------------------------------
 - Adding support for Python 3.15.
 
+- Fixed `QuotedString` silently discarding white space in its quote strings, so
+  that `QuotedString("\n;", multiline=True)` behaved as if it had been defined
+  with just `";"`. Quote strings are no longer stripped, and if the opening
+  quote string starts with white space, those characters are removed from the
+  expression's whitespace chars so they are not skipped over before the opening
+  quote is matched. Quote strings that are entirely white space (and so could
+  never match) still raise `ValueError`, and a quote string containing a line
+  end no longer lets the quoted body span lines when `multiline` is `False`.
+  Issue #492.
+
 - Fixed `pyparsing_common.as_datetime` raising `Invalid date/time: microsecond
   must be in 0..999999` for valid ISO-8601 timestamps whose fractional seconds
   round up to a full second (e.g. `2021-06-15T12:30:59.9999995`, common in
